# DuetSoftwareFramework packages from a separately published build of our
# own, installed in place of the Duet3D archive's.
#
# One line per package:
#
#   <package> sha256:<checksum of the published .deb> <https location>
#
# The DSF packages pin each other to one exact version and check it again at
# runtime, so a build of our own is installed as a whole: every package that
# pkg/build.sh --packages=progs,meta produces in the fork, at a version
# <dsf.version>+<suffix> (3.7.0~rc.1+mp.1 for a modified 3.7.0~rc.1). Only
# these packages are taken from the build; duetsd, duetwebcontrol and
# reprapfirmware come from the archive, where the build's meta package pins
# them. An empty list installs the archive's packages. Only a published build
# is taken, checked against the pin: no local path, no fallback, a mismatch
# stops the build. See "Installing a DuetSoftwareFramework build of our own"
# in the README.
#
# A board firmware file is not a package of the build; it goes through
# firmware.list.

# 3.7.0-rc.1+mp.7: numbered G-code lines (N...) may end with an RRF-style
# checksum, '*' plus 1-3 digits as XOR or exactly 5 digits as CRC-16/XMODEM.
# Jobs, macros, code streams and HTTP/IPC codes check it; a wrong or malformed
# checksum raises a parser error that aborts a running job or macro, no resend
# is requested. mp.6 brought the upstream fix that keeps the object model in
# step after an SPI transfer timeout, with our key comparison on top.
